                <pb facs="0094" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.H Continental Solidarity/94: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hull</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-21T20:00:00-05:00">December 21, 1938—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>87. My 84, December 21, 3 p.m. The President requested me to read the text of the
                    declaration in Cabinet meeting this afternoon and he expressed his entire
                    approval of the formula proposed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
